window.docContents[119].resolve({"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/How-a-definition-reads-___-the-rendering-family/#annotation-pkc-math-symbol":{"contents":"Overrides every naming heuristic for one token.\n\nattribute [pkc_math_symbol \"n_{d}\"]  MironovNK.nd\nattribute [pkc_math_symbol \"m_{vt}\"] MironovNK.mvt\n\n\nThis is not always cosmetic. The rendering heuristic maps a Greek-letter spelling to its letter, so\na refractive-index field named nu would typeset as  — an angular frequency. Notation stated\nonce, on the field, wins over every heuristic, and the index below is therefore a table of the places\nwhere a heuristic was deliberately overruled.\n\n* Declaration* Renders as* Layout* avsForward* \\sigma^0* function head* byPolarization* P* function head* columns* J* function head* combined* D* function head* decay* \\tau* function head* grad* \\nabla* prefix operator* letExample* q* function head* model* F* function head* noted* \\gamma* function head* residual* R* function head* scaled* g* function head* scaledByTwo* u* function head* shared* S* function head* twiceBound* T* function head\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Using the library: annotations and generated indexes\u0009How a definition reads — the rendering family","header":"31.8.2. @[pkc_math_symbol]  — fix the notation","id":"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/How-a-definition-reads-___-the-rendering-family/#annotation-pkc-math-symbol"},"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/Where-the-calculus-is-left-___-the-boundary-family/#annotation-kindConst":{"contents":"The third mint tier, and the one a nullary crossing candidate turns out to be. Where\n@[kindCrossing] goes from an already-kinded value and @[kindIngest] admits external data\nthrough a check, @[kindConst] mints from neither: the value is adjudicated data — a cited\ncoefficient table, a configuration bound or box, a seed, a threshold, or a structural constant of\nthe model such as a zero accumulator or the vacuum index 1.\n\n/-- The probe's adjudicated threshold, cited to the table it is read from. -/\n@[kindConst]\ndef probeThreshold : Quantity outputKind Float := ⟨0.02⟩\n\n\nThe mint's value is data rather than dataflow, so its provenance is the declaration's docstring\nrather than its signature — there is no argument to trace it to. That is why the tier exists as its\nown tag instead of collapsing into @[kindCrossing]: a declaration with no kinded argument is\ndefinitionally this tier, having nothing to cross from, and the crossing attribute's rejection\nmessage names it for exactly that reason.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Using the library: annotations and generated indexes\u0009Where the calculus is left — the boundary family","header":"31.3.3. @[kindConst]  — a constant mint","id":"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/Where-the-calculus-is-left-___-the-boundary-family/#annotation-kindConst"}});